WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.850
Two trays hold twenty counters altogether.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.890
Move three counters from the left tray to the right.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.510
The total stays twenty.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.990
Watch the gap: one side loses three at the same moment

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.570
the other side gains three.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.910
Start with twelve on the left and eight on the right.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:17.890
Move one across.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.170
The counts become eleven and nine.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.490
The difference shrinks from four to two.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.450
A single transfer changed the gap by two.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.730
Two storage cases hold forty eight badges.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.030
After six badges move from the fuller case to the other,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.010
the cases contain equal numbers.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.250
How many badges were in each case before the move?

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.080
Equal shares of forty eight are twenty four each.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.670
Put the six badges back into the fuller case and remove

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.640
them from the other.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.500
Thirty and eighteen are the original counts.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.180
Their difference is twelve, exactly twice the transfer.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.660
Three trays contain thirty six counters.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.860
The first tray gives half its counters to the second.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.770
Then the second gives one third of its new pile

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:05.520
to the third.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.180
All three finish equal.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.460
How many counters started in the first,

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:10.980
second and third trays?

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.810
Finish with twelve in every tray.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.510
The second tray kept two thirds of its pile.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.110
Those two thirds are twelve, so each third is six.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.610
Just before that transfer the second tray held eighteen,

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.670
and the third held only six.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:30.830
The first still held twelve.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.610
The first tray kept half and ended with twelve.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.060
It must have started with twenty four and passed twelve

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:38.790
to the second.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:40.830
Remove those twelve from eighteen.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.770
The starting counts were twenty four, six and six.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.450
Run both transfers forwards to check.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.330
The words its new pile matter.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.030
A fraction acts on the contents at that moment.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.950
Mark the total, record who gives and receives,

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.340
and run transfers backwards one at a time when the final

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.270
amounts are known.
